From 8f155cae39b3196cfe66a9032fdec3fcb1fe484f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mowlya Shree Manjunatha <mowlyamanjunath@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 04:39:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(agents): add PDS retrieval keyed to date of loss
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The policy agent selects the PDS version in force on the claim's
date_of_loss and returns clause text for it, never the version in
force today. Retrieval takes no "today" parameter at all, so a
caller cannot get this wrong by passing the wrong date — a claim
notified months after the loss, and decided later still, must be
read under the wording the customer actually held.

Insuring clauses match on peril. Exclusions only surface when the
caller supplies a signal for the fact that triggers them (an
unlicensed driver, gradual damage), keeping the boundary from
ADR-0002: this agent matches known facts to clause text, it does not
establish the facts or decide whether they mean the claim is
excluded.

The regression test the build plan calls for is
test_retrieves_the_pds_in_force_at_date_of_loss_not_today, using two
motor PDS versions that both define clause 7.2 with different
wording so a wrong-version bug is observable, not theoretical.
